#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:4
msgid "PD separation"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Prefill/Decode (PD) separation is available in the community edition. "
"Prefill replicas compute prompt KV cache; decode replicas reuse it through "
"Xavier or native NIXL and produce the response. Requests are scheduled "
"round-robin within each role. No enterprise package or License is required."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:12
msgid "Launch"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:14
msgid ""
"For Xavier, use NVIDIA GPUs and a reachable host address (not ``0.0.0.0``). "
"The V1 connector requires vLLM 0.21.0 or newer. The existing V0 Xavier "
"adapter is retained for vLLM versions below 0.11.0; versions 0.11 through "
"0.20 are not supported by this V1 connector. GPU integration CI pins vLLM "
"0.21.0."
msgstr "Xavier: "

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:19
msgid ""
"The example starts one prefill replica on GPU 0 and one decode replica on "
"GPU 1. Replace the worker address with the full ``ip:port`` reported by "
"``client.get_workers_info()``. Both replicas must use the same model and "
"engine configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:51
msgid ""
"The same ``replica_config`` is accepted by ``POST /v1/models``, the async "
"Python client, and the CLI ``--replica_config`` JSON option. In the Web UI, "
"select vLLM, enable per-replica placement, and choose Prefill or Decode for "
"each replica. The community launch path defaults to Xavier when P/D roles "
"appear."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid "CLI launch"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:59
msgid "Start a local server first, or use an existing supervisor endpoint:"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:65
msgid "In another terminal, launch a 1P+1D deployment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:78
msgid ""
"Replace ``WORKER_ADDRESS`` with the worker's registered address, including "
"its actor port (shown in the worker startup log), not the HTTP API port. For"
" workers on different machines, use each worker's own address and GPU "
"indices. ``--replica_config`` is an alias for ``--replica-config``. The "
"replica count is inferred from the array length; no separate Xavier switch "
"is needed. Do not combine per-replica placement with global ``--n-gpu``, "
"``--gpu-idx``, or ``--worker-ip``. Invalid PD roles or incomplete P/D "
"topology fail before the launch request is sent."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:88
msgid "Configuration rules"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:90
msgid ""
"``replica`` is the total number of P and D replicas. At least one of each "
"role is required; more than one of either role is supported."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:92
msgid ""
"Omitted roles default to ``hybrid`` (ordinary replicas). A PD deployment "
"cannot mix hybrid replicas with P/D replicas."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Each entry specifies one worker and its GPU allocation. Different replicas "
"may run on different workers. Per-replica placement cannot be combined with "
"global ``worker_ip``, ``gpu_idx`` or ``n_gpu``, or cross-worker sharding "
"within a replica (``n_worker > 1``)."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:98
msgid ""
"``vllm_transfer_backend_type`` (alias ``transfer_backend_type``) selects "
"``xavier`` (default) or ``nixl``. Unknown backend names are rejected."
msgstr ""
"``vllm_transfer_backend_type`` (alias ``transfer_backend_type``) seleziona "
"``xavier`` (predefinito) o ``nixl``. I nomi di backend sconosciuti vengono "
"rifiutati."

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:101
msgid ""
"The topology is fixed for the deployment lifetime. To change its size or "
"roles, terminate the model and relaunch it with the new configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:105
msgid "Inference and lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:107
msgid ""
"Send ordinary OpenAI-compatible chat/completion requests to the base model "
"UID. Streaming and non-streaming requests use the same PD route. The prefill"
" subrequest uses one output token without changing the decode request's "
"generation settings. Routing becomes available only after all replicas and "
"transfer components are ready. Aborting a request reaches both roles. "
"Terminating a deployment also removes its router, rank-zero coordinator, "
"collective manager, and block tracker."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:115
msgid "Verification"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:117
msgid "On a machine with two free NVIDIA GPUs and the pinned vLLM environment, run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:124
msgid ""
"This test launches a community deployment in real subprocesses with one GPU "
"per role. It checks streaming and non-streaming responses, repeated prompts,"
" and four concurrent requests, requires both producer staging and decoder "
"KV-load log evidence, and terminates the deployment. To use locally cached "
"weights, set ``XINFERENCE_TEST_PD_MODEL_PATH``, "
"``XINFERENCE_TEST_PD_MODEL_NAME``, and ``XINFERENCE_TEST_PD_MODEL_SIZE`` to "
"the model path and its registered model name and size. The manually "
"triggered ``PD GPU integration`` GitHub Actions workflow runs the same test "
"on a selected runner with two GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:134
msgid "Hybrid/recurrent attention limitation"
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:136
msgid ""
"Xavier PD currently rejects hybrid/recurrent attention caches, including "
"Qwen3.5. The transferred implementation does not yet reliably preserve their"
" recurrent state across prefix-cache reuse and concurrent requests. Use "
"ordinary single instances for these models, or a full-attention model such "
"as Qwen3 for PD. Successful launch alone is not evidence of correct hybrid-"
"state transfer."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:143
msgid "Xavier V1 supported configurations and cache safety"
msgstr "Xavier "

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:145
msgid ""
"The V1 connector currently requires one GPU per replica (TP=1, PP=1), text-"
"only models, and no LoRA adapters. Multimodal models, prompt embeddings and "
"salted prompts are rejected until their cache identities and partitioning "
"are supported."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:149
msgid ""
"CPU snapshots are keyed by prompt content rather than reusable GPU block "
"IDs. Readers reserve complete snapshots during transfer; cache pressure or a"
" missing snapshot falls back to local computation. The number of retained "
"CPU blocks is bounded by the engine's KV block capacity. CPU memory can "
"approach the GPU KV cache size (twice that size for BF16 transported as "
"FP32), in addition to in-flight transfer buffers. Only complete layers are "
"published for remote reuse."
msgstr ""

#: source/user_guide/pd_separation.rst:156
msgid ""
"The connector handles block-first and K/V-first attention cache layouts. A "
"layout whose block axis cannot be identified safely is rejected. V0 prefill "
"replicas release only the requested completed sequence; ordinary hybrid and "
"decode replicas retain normal automatic cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid "Native NIXL backend"
msgstr "Backend NIXL nativo"

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid ""
"Set ``vllm_transfer_backend_type=\"nixl\"`` in the launch example to use "
"vLLM's native NixlConnector. Install ``nixl`` in the model environment "
"together with vLLM 0.21.0 or newer. The initial integration supports text-"
"only models without LoRA and requires TP=1, PP=1 and DP=1 per replica. "
"Multiple P and D replicas are supported. Xavier remains the default backend."
msgstr ""
"Impostare ``vllm_transfer_backend_type=\"nixl\"`` nell’esempio di avvio per "
"usare NixlConnector nativo di vLLM. Installare ``nixl`` e vLLM 0.21.0 o "
"successivo nell’ambiente del modello. L’integrazione iniziale supporta "
"modelli testuali senza LoRA con TP=1, PP=1 e DP=1 per replica e più repliche"
" P e D. Xavier resta il backend predefinito."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid ""
"Xinference allocates a separate NIXL side-channel port for each replica and "
"passes the producer's KV handoff metadata to the selected decoder. NIXL "
"manages transfer completion and cache release; failed handoffs fail the "
"request instead of silently recomputing. If a decoder never consumes a "
"completed prefill, vLLM's ``VLLM_NIXL_ABORT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT`` bounds "
"producer cache retention. Worker addresses must be reachable between "
"replicas, and the network must allow the allocated side-channel ports. This "
"path does not create Xavier collective actors or force eager execution."
msgstr ""
"Xinference assegna a ogni replica una porta del canale laterale NIXL e passa"
" i metadati KV del produttore al decoder selezionato. NIXL gestisce "
"completamento del trasferimento e rilascio della cache. Un passaggio fallito"
" causa un errore anziché un ricalcolo silenzioso. Se nessun decoder consuma "
"il prefill completato, ``VLLM_NIXL_ABORT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT`` di vLLM limita la"
" conservazione della cache del produttore. Indirizzi dei worker e porte "
"assegnate devono essere raggiungibili fra repliche. Questo percorso non crea"
" attori collettivi Xavier né impone l’esecuzione eager."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid ""
"For a reproducible comparison, run ``python benchmark/benchmark_pd.py "
"--help`` from the repository root. Supply a launch JSON containing model "
"settings and P/D replica placement, and a JSONL workload of chat request "
"bodies. The runner compares ordinary hybrid replicas, Xavier and NIXL "
"sequentially using the same GPU allocation and workload. It saves per-"
"request results, TTFT, average time per output token after the first token "
"(TPOT), latency percentiles and throughput under the specified latency "
"limits. Repeated workload entries measure warm prefix reuse; use distinct "
"prefixes for cold-cache measurements. Two GPUs cover 1P1D versus two hybrid "
"replicas; 2P2D requires four independent replica GPUs."
msgstr ""
"Per un confronto riproducibile, eseguire ``python benchmark/benchmark_pd.py "
"--help`` dalla radice del repository. Fornire un JSON di avvio con "
"impostazioni del modello e collocazione P/D, e un JSONL di richieste chat. "
"Il programma confronta in sequenza repliche ibride, Xavier e NIXL con le "
"stesse GPU e lo stesso carico. Salva risultati individuali, TTFT, tempo "
"medio per token di output dopo il primo (TPOT), percentili di latenza e "
"throughput entro i limiti specificati. Le ripetizioni misurano il riuso dei "
"prefissi caldi; usare prefissi diversi per cache fredde. Due GPU consentono "
"1P1D contro due repliche ibride; 2P2D richiede quattro GPU indipendenti."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:67
msgid ""
"For vLLM 0.21.0, GPU CI pins NIXL 1.1.0. Match the vLLM, Torch and NIXL "
"versions; importing vLLM alone does not validate engine startup."
msgstr ""
"Per vLLM 0.21.0, la CI GPU fissa NIXL 1.1.0. Usare versioni compatibili di "
"vLLM, Torch e NIXL; importare vLLM non basta a verificare l’avvio del "
"motore."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:66
msgid "Native PD currently requires ``n=1`` per request. Parallel sampling is rejected because its child requests cannot safely share one producer transfer lease."
msgstr "Il PD nativo richiede attualmente ``n=1`` per richiesta. Il campionamento parallelo viene rifiutato perché le richieste figlie non possono condividere in sicurezza un lease di trasferimento del produttore."

msgid ""
"For NIXL, wildcard worker binds are supported through automatic host "
"discovery. Set ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST`` in launch ``envs`` or the "
"worker environment to select a reachable interface; launch ``envs`` take "
"precedence. If discovery fails or returns loopback, configure this variable "
"explicitly. Xinference always replaces ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT`` with "
"a dynamically allocated port per replica, including on recovery. A fixed "
"side-channel port is not supported; firewalls must allow dynamic ports "
"between replica hosts."
msgstr ""
"NIXL supporta il binding wildcard del worker tramite rilevamento automatico "
"dell’host. Impostare ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST`` negli ``envs`` di avvio"
" o nell’ambiente del worker per scegliere un’interfaccia raggiungibile; gli "
"``envs`` di avvio hanno precedenza. Se il rilevamento fallisce o restituisce"
" loopback, impostare esplicitamente la variabile. Xinference sostituisce "
"sempre ``VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT`` con una porta dinamica per replica, "
"anche durante il ripristino. Le porte fisse non sono supportate; i firewall "
"devono consentire porte dinamiche tra gli host delle repliche."

msgid ""
"The GPU test runs both Xavier and NIXL; install ``nixl`` alongside the "
"pinned vLLM version. Xavier verification requires producer staging and "
"decoder load logs. NIXL verification requires ``calling _read_blocks`` and "
"completed receive logs, including all four concurrent requests."
msgstr ""
"Il test GPU esegue Xavier e NIXL; installare ``nixl`` insieme alla versione "
"fissata di vLLM. Xavier richiede log di staging del produttore e di "
"caricamento del decoder. NIXL richiede ``calling _read_blocks`` e log di "
"ricezione completata per tutte e quattro le richieste simultanee."

msgid ""
"Native NIXL replicas are not replayed automatically after a worker restart "
"because their routing state belongs to the supervisor. Relaunch the "
"deployment after a worker restart. Recovery of a model subprocess on a live "
"worker re-registers its PD route."
msgstr ""
"Le repliche NIXL native non vengono ripristinate automaticamente dopo il "
"riavvio di un worker, poiché lo stato di routing appartiene al supervisore. "
"Riavviare la distribuzione dopo il worker. Il ripristino di un sottoprocesso"
" del modello su un worker attivo registra nuovamente la sua rotta PD."

#: user_guide/pd_separation.rst:57
msgid ""
"For Xavier diagnostics, set ``XINFERENCE_XAVIER_PROFILE=1`` in the model "
"process environment and collect server logs. Run ``python "
"benchmark/analyze_pd_profile.py server.log --output profile.json`` to "
"summarize GPU copy, actor RPC and Gloo receive timings. Profiling "
"synchronizes CUDA and adds logging overhead; run it separately from "
"throughput benchmarks. Timings are nested: ``load_rpc`` includes actor "
"timings, and ``actor_receive`` includes ``gloo_receive``. Do not add nested "
"totals or interpret Gloo receive wait as isolated network time."
msgstr ""
"Per diagnosticare Xavier, impostare ``XINFERENCE_XAVIER_PROFILE=1`` "
"nell’ambiente del processo del modello e raccogliere i log del server. "
"Eseguire ``python benchmark/analyze_pd_profile.py server.log --output "
"profile.json`` per riepilogare i tempi di copia GPU, RPC degli actor e "
"ricezione Gloo. La profilazione sincronizza CUDA e aggiunge costi di "
"logging; eseguirla separatamente dai benchmark di throughput. I tempi sono "
"annidati: ``load_rpc`` include i tempi degli actor e ``actor_receive`` "
"include ``gloo_receive``. Non sommare i totali annidati né interpretare "
"l’attesa di ricezione Gloo come tempo di rete isolato."
